  "question": "Yurt Reservation System at Pacific Trails Resort\n\n1) Background / Context\n\nPacific Trails Resort offers unique accommodations with yurts available for booking. The challenge is to develop a robust database system to manage yurt reservations, ensuring efficient tracking of availability and customer information.\n\n2) Objectives\n\n- Design and implement a database in 3NF to manage yurt reservations.\n- Enable functionality for customers to book yurts by selecting check-in and check-out dates.\n- Track and manage yurt availability and customer details efficiently.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Stakeholders: Resort Management, IT Department.\n- Users: Customers, Resort Staff.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Allow customers to check availability and book a specific yurt for desired dates.\n- Record customer personal information, including first name, last name, email, and phone number.\n- Track specific yurt attributes such as number of beds, maximum occupancy, smoking preference, pet-friendliness, and nightly cost.\n- Facilitate the search for available yurts on desired dates.\n- Support creation of reservations linking customers to specific yurts and date ranges.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Ensure the database adheres to 3NF for optimal data organization and retrieval.\n- Data integrity must be maintained, particularly for foreign key relationships across tables.\n- Design should support scalability to accommodate growing demand and future expansion of yurt offerings.\n- Ensure system availability and reliability, with minimal downtime for reservation functionalities.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0167\nCREATE TABLE `customers` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `first_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(25) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `email` (`email`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `yurts` (\n  `yurt_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `yurt_name` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `number_of_beds` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `maximum_occupancy` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `smoking_allowed` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `pet_friendly` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  `nightly_cost` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`yurt_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `yurt_name` (`yurt_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `reservations` (\n  `reservation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `yurt_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `check_in_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `check_out_date` date NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`reservation_id`),\n  KEY `customer_id` (`customer_id`),\n  KEY `yurt_id` (`yurt_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `reservations_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customers` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `reservations_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`yurt_id`) REFERENCES `yurts` (`yurt_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
